  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & ={d}_{11}{C}_{11}+{d}_{12}{C}_{12}+{d}_{13}{C}_{13}+{d}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+1\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1{C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & \u2217 & \u2217 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & \u2217 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & \u2217 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3 & \u2217\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-1)^{1+4}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1(0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}|) \\\\  & =-(0-4(3\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6)+0) \\\\  & =-48\\end{aligned}\n$$",
